    <decisions>
        <description>Second-line guard after the picker. Catches Fully Refunded (Screen_Already_Refunded) and non-Paid (Screen_Not_Paid) gifts if the lookup surfaces them anyway. Fundraising Cloud rejects GiftRefund inserts against non-Paid GTs at the platform layer.</description>
        <name>Decision_Already_Refunded</name>
        <label>Refundable?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Screen_Refund_Details</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Refundable</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>YesAlreadyRefunded</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>frmIsAlreadyRefunded</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Screen_Already_Refunded</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes — already refunded</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>NotPaid</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>frmNotPaid</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Screen_Not_Paid</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Not yet paid</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Short-circuits when the donor has no refundable gifts so staff see a clean explanation rather than an empty data table. Checks Get_Donor_Refundable_GTs.Id for null (works on both single-record and empty-collection queries).</description>
        <name>Decision_Any_Refundable</name>
        <label>Any refundable gifts?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Screen_Pick_Gift</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Has refundable gifts</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>NoneRefundable</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Donor_Refundable_GTs</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Screen_No_Refundable</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>None refundable</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Screen flow launched from the donor Account record page via the FQS Refund Donor Gift quick action. Presents the donor&apos;s refundable Gift Transactions (Status = Paid with a positive outstanding balance) in a picker, then creates a Gift Refund with Status = Completed against the picked gift. Fundraising Cloud handles the downstream cascade automatically (Gift Transaction Current Amount, Refunded Amount, Status = Fully Refunded on full refunds, and Gift Transaction Designation Amount proration).

Pre-flight guards catch three edge cases with clean explanation screens: (1) the donor has zero refundable gifts, (2) the picked gift is already Fully Refunded, (3) the picked gift is not in Paid status. Fee-reversal fields appear only when the picked gift carries non-zero gateway or processor fees.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmExternalId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;FQS-GR-&quot; &amp; {!pickedGtId} &amp; &quot;-&quot; &amp; TEXT({!$Flow.CurrentDateTime})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmHasFees</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>OR(
  BLANKVALUE({!Get_GT.ProcessorTransactionFee}, 0) &gt; 0,
  BLANKVALUE({!Get_GT.GatewayTransactionFee}, 0) &gt; 0
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmIsAlreadyRefunded</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>OR(
  {!Get_GT.CurrentAmount} &lt;= 0,
  ISPICKVAL({!Get_GT.Status}, &quot;Fully Refunded&quot;)
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmNotPaid</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>AND(
  NOT(ISPICKVAL({!Get_GT.Status}, &quot;Paid&quot;)),
  BLANKVALUE({!Get_GT.RefundedAmount}, 0) &lt;= 0,
  {!Get_GT.CurrentAmount} &gt; 0
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmRefundAmount</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>{!refundAmount}</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmReverseGatewayFee</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!frmHasFees}, {!reverseGatewayFee}, 0)</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frmReverseProcessorFee</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!frmHasFees}, {!reverseProcessorFee}, 0)</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
